  "sentence_count": 22,
  "records": [
    {
      "id": "i01",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "At high redshift, metallicity relations can disagree because galaxies evolved, or because calibrations changed the measuring scale.",
      "text_sha256": "98576329a813fc85aa03e8ced4932c86adea7a0ae90c2f152f915f5ae01cafe6",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/i01-98576329a813.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "116ef13c9d06b3ecbe718272a3e808a006e61d0a257adc6effa74622255acb5e",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.328000",
          "size": "133248"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i02",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "If the relation genuinely evolved, that would be a fact about the enrichment history of young galaxies.",
      "text_sha256": "d2dfb907ea6d2ca52d17fdfd8be99a10877e50c647a07d2238ae44a3fe782cf2",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/i02-d2dfb907ea6d.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "81b0ef983a7e973df0e7db34e7ba50dc0f1c359c7a6d007de0c4f8cb82941b0d",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "5.136000",
          "size": "82176"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i03",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "But an apparent offset could instead be a fact about strong-line recipes, reference frames, or scale conversions rather than galaxies.",
      "text_sha256": "9080d8241dd340610575c9b222e4bada7cdf0b7ce222e0bdc9ff5a48d67df53e",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/i03-9080d8241dd3.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "0203dd5bf4884cd773305b62a2d0cad73e38da841b40907f7e993dc26b54bf02",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.272000",
          "size": "116352"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "i04",
      "section": "motivation",
      "text": "How do we tell evolution from calibration?",
      "text_sha256": "99dc49654f8e5bff440bb011130b3597da0fe8ee730f200726faf99b32f32b3f",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/i04-99dc49654f8e.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "6334f51ac81cad4d1790183e9d3e294d24efd3e0b469ca2de0be68b47fb787a8",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "2.640000",
          "size": "42240"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d01",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "Counting metallicity rows cannot settle that question, because a table entry is not yet a direct-temperature anchor on a common scale.",
      "text_sha256": "d93c5467415c804f0f2c8a7acf2c13283409970c73f2bfe24b882f45d489bb2b",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/d01-d93c5467415c.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "670fa326e42facdf2b5add1137fc7a95d4aaf31dcb1e5e8975af7c9de3ad259e",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.960000",
          "size": "111360"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "d02",
      "section": "difficulty",
      "text": "Even an auroral-line label is insufficient without flux uncertainty, abundance-capable companion lines, stellar mass, and provenance that can reproduce the derivation.",
      "text_sha256": "c9330eee26b7c7c1a8119a7a84e06cc8e8857625cfcadeefc3179cbd3aeafb86",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/d02-c9330eee26b7.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "933be3186d0f63079c79ab9697b51bce92c828fb54b8f8f31ec7b6e0d6bec193",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.432000",
          "size": "150912"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p01",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "The discriminating chain begins with a source-published auroral flux and uncertainty, judged under one predeclared quality rule.",
      "text_sha256": "a885e3699cb80400a6536ce444532fba89230205a347b609aa09f2b2f7616bc8",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/p01-a885e3699cb8.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "f9e32ab51af9598430941ee727d42486fd6491c3ece84f70080d69ef136aaa8a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.728000",
          "size": "123648"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p02",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "A frozen line-ratio pipeline then carries the accepted fluxes into electron temperature without selecting a convenient recipe after inspection.",
      "text_sha256": "2ef810334c5f32d9f950defb7293d286f7c36488aa24a7e7bd9d399e09097098",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/p02-2ef810334c5f.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "97f26499a045944a935e61c47d44fb9f3e9ea5e8442179a2656c2a711251fc68",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.400000",
          "size": "134400"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p03",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "That temperature becomes a direct oxygen abundance only when the required ionic channels survive, while every refusal stays explicit.",
      "text_sha256": "615e148ab52767181a4b61bfd50d7eaefbdf6461625d10f404aac511754c47a1",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/p03-615e148ab527.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "7abaa0708dd3ea0cb7cf0bd84098c34101c70184db4f611a03e8a0021488f678",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.496000",
          "size": "135936"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p04",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "The direct abundance is joined to the same object's stellar mass and projected onto one declared direct-temperature reference scale.",
      "text_sha256": "c119e0c4dfd035f97c6c428143b4648642555cfff2e743caa5c0844d8b92eb92",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/p04-c119e0c4dfd0.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "0c074a7b9bbf4c4c071c4f45b0a9a31d55c92261c0ef2cc58e9bc5e2d431a3a0",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.008000",
          "size": "112128"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "p05",
      "section": "peak",
      "text": "Only after seam, lensing, and scale controls pass can the common-scale comparison ask which explanation fits, without answering it in this canary.",
      "text_sha256": "87f84b154c294098e7094950bbdeb0961044a1b8163b625bfa2170b5ee1e6ff3",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/p05-87f84b154c29.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "ac5279d23d71bbae793eb6824c7a3e0eef3aca8e9d47709cd9093fb9781a061e",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.240000",
          "size": "147840"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f01",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "The source ledger preserves enumeration, candidate rows, contract-grade anchors, and matched-mass bins as changing units, with every result count removed here.",
      "text_sha256": "1d6b39093b433a644bedd445203bf299218329583a024de2b27cc72f74265536",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/f01-1d6b39093b43.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2d9278e919394f426435edd7a4e820d6b85f97ce9e667e138c32985faeb3abce",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.216000",
          "size": "147456"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "f02",
      "section": "sample",
      "text": "Because no sibling source freeze exists, the method keeps the pipeline stages but drops table totals, anchor totals, mass-bin occupancy, and every derived value.",
      "text_sha256": "bb927a4f74bfb3ad17a0dd05403301cc807f4b7521fd1c406403f73d1dcb0682",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/f02-bb927a4f74bf.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "2d515e71f4481280f909c166888c176ff698906ca859ee8a2f9b4fd422523ba1",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.600000",
          "size": "153600"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e01",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "The estimator is a common-scale direct-abundance difference at matched stellar mass, built symbolically and left unevaluated.",
      "text_sha256": "2e71a714523129b41b9990b46c363d83eb3d19c1b2feea4842b483fabd3c0679",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/e01-2e71a7145231.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "8413b0834f7463a04e574cef3260392b185369dae3b14cb976b1d04b42d83f74",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.224000",
          "size": "115584"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "e02",
      "section": "estimator",
      "text": "Scale uncertainty travels beside statistical uncertainty, so a visual offset cannot silently become a physical-evolution claim.",
      "text_sha256": "e20a6f7e38475929e2e011840fc0ee24d9133282be1958155f3e331e329c93dc",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/e02-e20a6f7e3847.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "425950637463de26b45bb4fd9675279d9f9fcf1b8019a05ec972bd01576f3bad",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "7.848000",
          "size": "125568"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c01",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "The auroral-quality control tests noise and blending, while the line-completeness control tests whether a temperature can become an abundance.",
      "text_sha256": "56081cf40aeee645579b618d9ed96642ff28848e8b8d79ae615df55bbc1ed949",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/c01-56081cf40aee.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "b069437e91a7e314524cb832e14dbd8dc1d533868eb3ebe3519d67a24d5839b7",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.376000",
          "size": "134016"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "c02",
      "section": "controls",
      "text": "The mass-join, lensing, and scale controls prevent the same derived abundance from supporting incompatible physical interpretations.",
      "text_sha256": "b705d7edf8478522f62a79567513a479863e113c214430f52371388c4f659a29",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/c02-b705d7edf847.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "64cb40366f4b7f7bfbc2afcc93561e6d5f75badc3ab118128c36b8b81bde398a",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.960000",
          "size": "111360"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g01",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "We tied our own hands by freezing anchor classes, quality rules, derivation physics, and the declared reference scale before computing any abundance.",
      "text_sha256": "8e2fce54dbf5fb3ffe549904de08f6dca4ce5c28be34864d83ad195f472faa87",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/g01-8e2fce54dbf5.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "a51f48adb59cc0603dc89f15049078c6bfd41e626c62cad40cabe48e6cd517c8",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.616000",
          "size": "137856"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "g02",
      "section": "discipline",
      "text": "The gates are scientific discipline: no missing flux, mass, magnification, or uncertainty can be repaired with an assumption chosen after inspection.",
      "text_sha256": "dac546a7822ec13e5b802e38bd640a7e468ff6fc170388f18740dc7ec91e7ed8",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/g02-dac546a7822e.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "9ff8a5c743e4bf405a87b72a5e650671fdb96f9200b0385d268cf5c802a3935e",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "8.112000",
          "size": "129792"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "b01",
      "section": "boundary",
      "text": "What is known is the anchor-building method; table counts, anchor yield, mass-bin occupancy, offset sign, and any evolution verdict remain outside this canary.",
      "text_sha256": "69a27abde6cf9310feb18f5d2092b45b97df68608ca60cf7dca0c9e6405387da",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/b01-69a27abde6cf.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "92e037ff3dd5c67f0c9696bb4e2d6de0f0c58a15f0a8cd5d4bb69378936279b2",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "9.504000",
          "size": "152064"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x01",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Ask the opening question again: would a common-scale offset belong to young galaxies, or to the calibration process?",
      "text_sha256": "fe0e38356eff81c19d96c1452d74f2a57373ac1d7d73878509c730178f38e340",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/x01-fe0e38356eff.mp3",
      "file_sha256": "258aaf9079277587d9a2de7e991c57d5bba5b809ddfdbbf7a684983e70e13c21",
      "probe": {
        "programs": [],
        "stream_groups": [],
        "streams": [
          {
            "codec_name": "mp3",
            "codec_type": "audio",
            "sample_rate": "24000",
            "channels": 1
          }
        ],
        "format": {
          "duration": "6.504000",
          "size": "104064"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "x02",
      "section": "payoff",
      "text": "Now we have a method that can separate those explanations without manufacturing an anchor count, an offset, or a result.",
      "text_sha256": "e940facf0a88e391f527c57342b2826261ea2aa384d3b2f7f80a90443be12e01",
      "file": "audio/mzr-anchor/raw/x02-e940facf0a88.mp3",
